# ORBITGENE runs on Neon Postgres in production. Nothing else is required:
# the app has no accounts, no third-party API keys, and no paid services.
#
# The only public data sources are keyless and public:
#   - UniProt REST   (uniprot.org)
#   - NCBI E-utilities (eutils.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov)
#   - NOAA SWPC JSON (services.swpc.noaa.gov)
#
# Copy to .env.local and fill in only what you need.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Production persistence (required in production)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Neon connection string. console.neon.tech -> your project -> Connection
# string. Keep it out of git; .env* is gitignored except this example file.
DATABASE_URL=postgresql://user:password@ep-xxxx-pooler.region.aws.neon.tech/neondb?sslmode=require

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Store selection
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# neon   - Neon/Postgres via DATABASE_URL. This is what production uses.
# pglite - an embedded Postgres that runs inside the Node process, backed by a
#          directory on disk. Zero setup for local development and CI, but the
#          data is not durable across a redeploy and it does not scale to more
#          than one process.
#
# Leave this unset to auto-select: pglite in development, neon in production.
# Set it to pglite in production only if you deliberately want a throwaway
# deployment.
# ORBITGENE_STORE=neon

# Where the embedded store keeps its files. Defaults to .orbitgene/pglite.
# ORBITGENE_PGLITE_DIR=.orbitgene/pglite